<title>UK: UK Aug global trade deficit 584 mln stg.</title>
<headline>UK Aug global trade deficit 584 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics issued the following data on Britain's global trade in July (in million stg, previously announced data in brackets)</p>
<p>    GLOBAL TRADE	     AUGUST   JULY   (PREL JULY)</p>
<p>    Trade balance		-584   -1,224    (-1,229)</p>
<p>    Exports		    13,933   13,804   (13,800)</p>
<p>    Imports		    14,517   15,028   (15,029)</p>
<p>    EU trade balance	     13     -505     (-541)</p>
<p>    EU exports		  7,919    7,732    (7,713)</p>
<p>    EU imports		  7,906    8,237    (8,254)</p>
<p>    TRADE VALUE EX OIL/ERRATICS    AUGUST   JULY   (PREL JULY)</p>
<p>    Trade balance (in million stg)     -1,183  -1,755   (-1,794)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (imports)  0.5%    0.5%     (0.5%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (exports)  1.0%    2.5%     (2.0%)</p>
<p>TRADE VOLUME EX OIL/ERRATICS</p>
<p>    Import volume index (base 1990) 126.9   129.6    (128.5)</p>
<p>    Export volume index (base 1990) 141.9   139.4    (139.0)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (imports)   2.0     0.5     (0.5%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on yr-ago qtr (imps)   8.0     8.0     (7.5%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (exports)   2.0     2.5     (2.5%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on yr-ago qtr (exps)   7.0     7.5     (7.5%)</p>
<p>    TRADE IN OIL (VALUE MLN STG)    AUGUST   JULY  (PREL JULY)</p>
<p>    BALANCE				   425     437	(465)</p>
<p>    EXPORTS				   859     882	(909)</p>
<p>    IMPORTS				   434     445	(444)</p>
<p>Economists had forecast a deficit of 1.0 billion stg.</p>
<p>The global trade gap excluding oil and erratic items such as ships, aircraft, precious stones and silver was 1,183 million stg in August versus 1,755 million stg in July.</p>
<p>The ONS said the global trend of the whole world goods deficit is narrowing.</p>
